% --- landscape
%  6. True landscape pages
%     LR4's own wide GC page has MediaBox [0 0 842 595.25] and NO /Rotate
%     entry: Word used a genuinely wider sheet and drew the header and footer on
%     it upright. pdflscape does the opposite (portrait sheet + /Rotate 90),
%     which lays the logo and footer on their side. So swap the physical page
%     registers instead. Two traps:
%       - geometry's \newgeometry flatly refuses paperwidth/paperheight keys, so
%         it cannot do this at all (and calls \clearpage internally on the way
%         in and out, which made the old fancyhdr footer vanish);
%       - the register is spelled differently per engine. pdfTeX and XeTeX want
%         \pdfpagewidth; LuaTeX renamed it to \pagewidth and merely warns at the
%         old spelling, while corrupting the page count.
%     Margins are absolute offsets from the page edge and survive the swap
%     untouched; \textwidth/\textheight — and \hsize, \vsize and \columnwidth,
%     which are what paragraphs, the page builder and float environments
%     actually measure against and which do NOT follow \textwidth — must be
%     reset by hand.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
